WEBVTT

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:08.860
We're fighting right now in the galaxy soccer tournament, Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.280
Our first opponent is the planet Sandorias.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.210
We continue to fight as we aim to be best in the universe.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.500
We will meet at the stadium.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:26.420
Tenma!

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.910
Shindou-san!

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.350
We looked everywhere for you guys!

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.890
We finally met up.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.340
What are those?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.410
We found them in town.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.020
We bought them for you, too.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:43.980
This one's for you, Aoi-san!

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.980
T-Thanks...

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:27.870
A soccer battle?

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.080
They surrounded us while we were touring the town.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.570
You'll find people like those lot anywhere.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.970
But I can't believe they would do things like that to us!

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.470
They kept trying to bodyslam us on purpose!

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.760
That's not soccer!

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:48.260
Well, they <i>did</i>  say they wanted to harm us.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.730
Yeah, but we're playing by the rules here! It's not fair!

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.660
The fate of all our planets is at stake in Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.830
If we lose, we have to surrender our planet.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.740
I can understand why they wouldn't welcome us, but to go that far...

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:11.540
But that Captain Kazelma guy said they'd fight fair and square.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.200
So it shouldn't be a problem.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.250
Even if they do try to cheat their way out of this...

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.470
I'll stop all of their shoots.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.910
That's right. Our main goalkeeper is Ibuki.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.210
It's not me.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.850
I shouldn't be surprised...

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.500
Ibuki's the one who's been defending the goal all this time.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:37.870
But I've been practicing every day too, to be part of the representative team!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.950
Leave it to me, Tenma!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.820
I'll protect the goal no matter what!

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.160
Is this guy trying to steal my position?

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.210
Try and steal it from me if you can.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.760
What is this?

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:16.440
Are you Kazelma Worg, the captain of the Sandorias Eleven?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.150
Who are you?

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.910
He's our assistance.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:20.750
Assistance?

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:22.040
That's right.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:27.080
The Queen of Falam Orbius sent him to us so we could win.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.410
He's strong, this guy.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.630
Strong?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.370
Then, those marks...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:43.340
I'm Barga Zacks, one of Falam Orbius's Shitennou. {バルガ・ザックス}

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.240
The Earth Eleven are no match for me.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.850
I'll crush them to pieces!

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.230
Thank you for your offer, but I will have to turn you down.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.830
What? Turn me down?

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.330
This is <i>our</i>  fight.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.450
We will fight with our own abilities.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.600
N-Now, hang on a minute, Kazelma!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.100
He says he's gonna make us win! You can't turn him down!

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.540
The prideful Sandorian, huh?

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.710
Now, to practice, everyone.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.870
If you want to practice, you're on your own.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.680
We're fighting with Barga.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.380
What?

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:30.770
What's more important to us right now isn't defending our pride.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.390
It's defending our home.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.140
This room is used for training?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.380
But how? There aren't even any goals.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.300
I'm done setting the system.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.220
A field?!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.370
It's a hologram.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.580
Hologram?

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:55.840
Yeah.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:58.030
But it's not just any hologram. {zanakurou is just standing there being quietly amazed. moe.}

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:03.590
It sends signals to our brains at the same time, to make it feel like the real thing to us.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.780
Like the real thing?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:11.280
You're right! It's like we're on real grass!

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.140
Is it the same for those, too, then?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.930
It's like the set changes we use between scenes in kabuki.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.650
It feels like a real goal!

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.070
Here, we can practice without anyone bothering us.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:25.360
Yeah!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:29.110
Okay then! Let's split up into offense and defense for practice!

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.340
Yeah!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.070
Hey.

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.140
I go first.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.700
You go over there and watch.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.510
Let's go.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.550
Move up, Matatagi!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.050
I'll stop you!

00:06:59.060 --> 00:06:59.690
He got through!

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.190
Good job, Matatagi!

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:04.060
Matatagi-kun used to be in track.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.190
He's the fastest runner on the team.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.680
With that dribble... To the right!

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.160
He blocked it!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.120
He predicted his next move.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.790
Minaho-kun's father used to be a prestigious detective.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.880
He's good at deducing what other people are thinking.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.320
From the right!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:25.750
I see!

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:26.750
Tetsukado-kun!

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:28.750
I'll stop you!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:37.600
Since Tetsukado-kun used to be a boxer, his strong point is making nimble movements that involve tight turns.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:43.500
Kusaka-kun used to be the leader of a gang, and he changes into a completely different person when he's mad.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.940
But that's because he was trying to hide his own weakness.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:47.690
It's mine!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.780
Wow!

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:58.950
Manabe-kun uses his extraordinary situational judgment and analytic skills to precisely calculate other people's moves.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:05.710
Konoha-chan is quiet and reserved, but she responds with amazing reflexes when she needs them.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.340
Zanakurou-kun is a famous kabuki actor and has incredible balance.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:18.470
Sakura-san does rhythmic gymnastics and her physical form is the best within the team.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.190
I memorized everyone's backgrounds, but...

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.940
They all keep getting stronger.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:29.660
Their progress grows so fast, it's almost unbelievable!

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.660
Our goalkeeper Ibuki-kun used to be a basketball player.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.450
As an athlete, he won't lose to anyone!

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:39.080
Come on!

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.240
Here I go!

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:44.920
Good, Ibuki!

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.380
I won't lose, either!

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:00.680
Shinsuke!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.600
I-I'm okay...

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.190
Is that it?

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.560
Raimon's goalkeeper isn't as impressive as they made you sound.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:15.740
Is the extent of his ability also within your expectations?

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.870
I couldn't block a single one.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.920
I guess I lose in terms of power...

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.680
Maybe I'm not cut out for this after all...

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:33.340
<i>Beast power?</i>

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.360
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:39.980
<i>I don't really understand it, but apparently we have it inside of us.</i>

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:43.900
<i>Shinsuke's feelings for soccer are as strong as ours.</i>

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.000
<i>I'm sure he'll be of help to us.</i>

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.770
<i>So please!</i>

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.660
Tenma...

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.990
I can't give up here!

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.780
Even if I don't have beast power, I'll get powerful the more that I train!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.200
Tenma begged the coach for me to stay here.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.710
I have to work hard for his sake, too!

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.170
Which is all well and good, but... How do I even work this thing?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.860
I should have asked them how to use it.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.400
Tetsukado!

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.240
Hey, Shinsuke.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.540
What are you doing here at this hour?

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.020
W-Well, I, uh...

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.940
Today's practice got to you, huh?

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:33.700
Okay then!

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.820
I'll join you!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.450
Let's train together and show Ibuki a thing or two!

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:40.910
Tetsukado!

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.820
Umm...

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.120
Hm, that's strange...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.280
I think I'm supposed to press here and here for the Hard course...

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.680
You don't know how to use it either?

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.800
Heh, I got it!

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.720
I-Is it okay?

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:04.680
It stopped.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.720
I guess.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.240
What is this?!

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:18.990
Now there's snow!

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.480
W-What's going on?

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.300
How should I know?

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:33.920
We're gonna crash!

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.250
Mom!

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.400
W-We're saved...

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.260
Ow...

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.460
A cave?

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:04.600
I don't remember seeing a hologram like this before.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.360
Then, did we break it?!

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.820
That's bad! We have to find a way out of here!

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:11.710
We can't.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.140
The Hard course is a back-to-back training menu that lasts for one hour.

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:18.550
Once you're in, you can't leave.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:20.550
C-Can't leave?!

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:21.710
Yeah.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:25.640
But you can also say that the menu ends after an hour.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.880
The room will change back to normal, and then we can start over again.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:32.020
It doesn't look like we'll manage proper training with this, anyway.

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:36.980
You're so carefree.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.960
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:45.420
Well, aren't you guys sparkly.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.620
'Cause we're Sparkly men.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:47.140
Right?

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:49.240
We've become sparkly cards for Galaxy.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:49.870
See?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.900
Whaaaat?

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.920
Well, we're Combo-technique-special men!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.420
That's right. We've become a super rare card.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.360
Whaaaat?

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:01.760
Don't get cocky, guys.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.160
It's Normal man!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.180
Who are you calling normal?!

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:05.300
I can become a special card t-

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.420
"Galaxy Cards Version 2 - Shine in Space! Earth Eleven!!"

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.080
On sale October 17th!

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:12.020
More on the web!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.740
Begin WARS!

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.480
Finally on the Nintendo 3DS!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.770
Send in your avatar to fight simulation battles!

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.320
What waits for you in WARS?

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.690
Danball Senki Wars!

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:26.990
Preorder it now!

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:31.080
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.080
Shinsuke!

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:36.920
Shinsuke?

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:38.940
Is he out?

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:41.710
Is Shinsuke here?

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.140
No, he's not. {just look at him sneakily turning the screen away, we all know what you're looking at}

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:47.720
Have you seen Shinsuke?

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.510
No, I haven't.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:53.100
That's weird...

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.020
Where did he go?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.700
I wanted to lend him this...

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.360
Could he be in the Black Room?

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:06.600
He <i>is</i>  here! Shinsuke's working hard!

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.580
All right then, I'll train with him!

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:12.540
What?

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.200
What is this?

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.160
It's all a mess!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.670
Why are you operating the Black Room system, Auntie?

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:26.710
I might not look like it, but I'm a scientist who specializes in virtual reality.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:32.220
Coach Kuroiwa asked me to participate in the Earth Eleven Support Project.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.560
I'm also the one who invented this Black Room.

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:37.480
You?!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.560
You're kidding!

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:43.600
It's completely locked down.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.570
It won't open for a while.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.380
Won't open?

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.980
That's how I'd made it to operate.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:51.720
No way...

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.440
Who is inside?

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.220
Tetsukado and Shinsuke.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.370
This is weird...

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.340
An hour has definitely passed by now...

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:06.300
Why won't it turn back?

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:09.260
Maybe I did break it...

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.720
Then does that mean we're stuck here forever?

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.220
Well, there's no point working ourselves up about it.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:19.620
This is the same as being stranded in the ocean.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:22.350
Sitting still and waiting for help to arrive is the best thing to do.

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.460
Tetsukado!

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:33.080
W-What?

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:36.620
What now?

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:38.920
Haniwa?

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:42.040
Why are they wearing uniforms?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.020
They're over here, too!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.540
W-What's with these things?

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:53.550
That's...

00:15:58.460 --> 00:15:59.640
What's happening?

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:03.100
The program has initiated a soccer battle.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.400
If they win this, it may unlock.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.900
But they need five people for a soccer battle.

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.920
They can't win with just the two of them.

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:13.110
Can't we do something?

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:15.990
Well, there's not much I can do from outside...

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.800
How about using virtual avatars?

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:19.450
Avatars?

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:25.170
The system contains our data, and it can bring up five people.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.590
It could be of some help to them that way.

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:32.360
Okay, I'll try it.

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:41.360
What do we do?

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.020
Guys!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.450
They're holograms.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.920
The Black Room has all of our data.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:53.530
It's using those versions of us.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:56.560
Either way, that means there's five of us here now!

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:04.580
Ibuki, switch with Shinsuke!

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.300
Ibuki!

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.060
For crying out loud...

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.300
Shinsuke, we're counting on you!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:22.560
Bring it!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:32.530
What?

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:39.030
Shinsuke!

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:45.710
Is this...?

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.300
If I continue to let those shoots in...

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:03.560
It's no use... I can't stop them...

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.270
They're too strong for me...

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:09.270
<i>Is that it?</i>

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:12.230
<i>Raimon's goalkeeper isn't as impressive as they made you sound.</i>

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:20.620
I won't lose!

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:27.080
Are you okay?

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.500
Y-Yeah...

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:32.220
They're planning to keep this up until we're crushed!

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:34.280
Anyway, you'll just have to hang in there!

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:35.740
We're counting on you, Shinsuke!

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.510
Wait, Tetsukado!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.970
I'll... switch with Ibuki.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.930
I'm not strong enough to stop them.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:48.380
Shinsuke...

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:59.360
I hate to admit it, but we need Ibuki to stop their shoots.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:11.880
Ibuki! No way!

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.750
Why can't he stop them?

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:26.070
He's strong enough to take them down...

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.770
His movements are getting smaller!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.520
Just like how I once did!

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:39.270
<i>What's going on here, Shinsuke?</i>

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:41.550
<i>You're lacking force.</i>

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.990
<i>Use stronger jumps!</i>

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:47.450
Don't move back!

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:49.830
Move up more and put all of your power into your jump!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:19:59.880
Yes!

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:00.840
We stopped it!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.340
We finally stopped it!

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:11.950
They vanished! We're saved!

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:12.680
Yeah!

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:14.450
All thanks to you!

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:15.930
Me?

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.310
Nice support!

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:20.900
Ibuki wouldn't have been able to do that without your advice!

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:25.750
How could I have been so mistaken?

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:30.370
We're on the same team, but all I kept thinking about was beating Ibuki.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.330
You're right.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.170
There's two of us here.

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:38.080
We just have to get stronger together!

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.840
Then, one day, I'll definitely catch up to him!

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:42.580
Yeah!

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.130
It changed back!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.560
Did the system fix itself?

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.060
Shinsuke! Tetsukado!

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.080
Guys!

00:20:57.080 --> 00:20:58.730
You two aren't hurt?

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.570
We're totally fine, as you can see.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:03.130
Thank goodness.

00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:05.550
Training by yourselves in secret...

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:06.570
Quit causing so much trouble.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:08.660
Sorry, Ibuki.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.030
I'll be more careful next time.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.380
Here is the stadium where your match with Sandorias will be held.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:26.420
Huh? This is the stadium?

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:28.930
There's nothing there...

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.210
Here it comes.

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:03.010
This is Starship Stadium, which can travel freely throughout the galaxy.

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:06.470
Over there, huh?

00:23:39.460 --> 00:23:43.020
The ferocity of the match intensifies as each side battles for their planet!

00:23:43.260 --> 00:23:46.190
Our team falters on an uncomfortable field of sand!

00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:49.550
Next, Clash! Space Soccer!!

00:23:49.550 --> 00:23:51.520
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:04.810
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:11.480
There's two of us here. We just have to get stronger together!

00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:12.410
That's all!
